Or, YAAP.  After playing Hack since around 1985 (?) I have gone on and off
the game.  Lately I was on a plane ride and started playing the newest
version to pass the time, and got hooked again.  It took a few weeks to get
a character good enough to make it.

I forgot to grab the final stats.  However Greg the chaoatic elven wizard
had (I think) St:18 Dx:22 Co:18 In:24 Wi:18 Ch:9

He started with a ring of slow digestion, which he put on in turn 1 and took
off maybe a total of 12 times.  Used a ring of regeneration 90% of the time,
else levitation when necessary and conflict a few times.  Things were so-so
until finding a bones level in the gnomish mines where a master lich was
wandering around (product of a poly trap on the level).  Had to whip out a
scroll of genocide or the game would've been over.  Found on the level all
kinds of goodies includes a silver dragon scale mail +2.  Came very close to
death on this level a few times.

Became much more powerful with the aide of the charm monster spell and a
magic whistle -- Probably the most inordinately powerful things you can get
as a wizard.  Poof - turn foes into friends.  Most often used spells:
Identify, Mapping, Charm, Healing (never found Extra), Magic Missile (deadly
as expert in that spell class), Remove Curse (only clerical spell I found).
Only had to write ID and Mapping myself, I found the rest.

By the time I reached the castle I had everything I needed, so I only wished
for magic markers.  Ended up with -40 AC, probably a record low for me.
Used only Magicbane as a weapon since I was using Charm/magic whistle as my
main tactic the whole game.  At -40AC I was practically unhittable anyway.

Ran into trouble only a few times.  Orcus town was very tough.  I had to
chase him up a few levels.  Ended up chasing a few demi-liches doing the
same thing.  Every time I saw the Wiz he lasted only a few steps since I
death-rayed him instantly.

I walked right through the elemental planes by detecting the exits and using
conflict to distract them while all while I ran flew across the rooms.  Took
off conflict before leaving the last level so as to not anger my god.
Instead I received an angel as a pet.

Came very close to death after fighting Death and going down to ~100 max HP
from about 170.  The only problem with my wizard using Magicbane is it takes
a lot of whacks to kill the tough stuff.  Meanwhile they summon summon away
and hem you in, so you can never hack your way out.  I ended up charming and
running, luckily I didn't run out of spell points.   At the very end I got
trapped by a gridlock of monsters with a big "L", master flayers and Death
closing in on me, so I wussed out and wrote blessed genocide scrolls for L
and h.  Sorry hobbits & dwarves.  I charmed some hostile priests to make
them friendly, and hid in the middle of the ant swarms they made since they
could do me no damage.

The correct altar was the first I found.  I had to leave behind my two pet
Jabberwocks, Jasper and Morgan though they served me well all through
Ghennom.  I forgot a large stash of gems or my score would have been better.
But who needs riches when you're immortal?

Hooray! Next I think I'll try Monk.

